vo_avfoundation: queue tvOS frames four refreshes ahead

On tvOS a layer shows a sample on the refresh its stamp asks for only when
it has the sample about three refreshes before that refresh, and a refresh
later otherwise. The video layer's limit and the OSD layer's differ: a
frame that reached them between 2.9 and 3.3 refreshes ahead showed its
subtitles a refresh before or after its picture. At 24 Hz queue-lead-ms's
128 ms is 3.1 refreshes, and frames reached the layers 2.8 to 3.9
refreshes ahead, depending on where mpv's target for them fell in the
refresh, which is set anew at every pause and seek: whether playback
desynced, and which way, looked random, and a pause or seek changed it
(plezy#3073).

On tvOS a display link now follows the display's refresh, and the queue
lead is at least four refreshes: 167 ms at 23.976 Hz, 160 ms at 25 Hz,
133 ms at 30 Hz. At 50 Hz and up queue-lead-ms (128 ms) is more and
stays, and so does the time a pause takes to show.

Apple TV 4K at 2160p 23.976 Hz, Plezy's options, the mode switch made
after the first frame as Plezy makes it; a 23.976 fps clip whose frames
and per-frame ASS events carry the same code in both halves of the
picture, captured over HDMI, a pause or a seek every 3 s. Stretches of
playback by the median time from enqueue to the refresh after the stamp:
below 2.9 refreshes 6 stretches, no frame mismatched; 2.9-3.35 refreshes
74 stretches, 72 frames mismatched a few at a time (49 with the
subtitles a refresh ahead, 23 behind); 3.35 refreshes and more 72
stretches, 2 frames. With stamps forced to other places in the refresh
the mismatches followed the same band. With a 170 ms lead: 40 stretches
4.0-4.8 refreshes ahead, no frame mismatched; with this patch: 77
stretches 3.8-4.7 refreshes ahead, none of 4429 frames mismatched. Left
as before: a frame or two around a seek, an unpause or a pause, and
stretches after a seek with the subtitles a refresh late throughout,
which come from where the stamps sit in the refresh at any lead (5 of
the 74 in the band, not counted above, stamped 74-85% of the way
through it; patch 0055).

